---@field members_can_use_personal_api_keys? boolean
---@field members_can_see_org_members? boolean When False, members (below admin) only see themselves in the members list and only project members in access control.
---@field allow_publicly_shared_resources? boolean
---@field read_only_mcp_access? boolean|distilled.Null When True, requests through the PostHog MCP server can read but not change this organization's data.
---@field member_notice? posthog.users.OrganizationMemberNotice|distilled.Null Notice shown in a banner to every member of the organization. Set to null to remove it.
---@field member_count? number
---@field is_ai_data_processing_approved? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field is_ai_training_opted_in? boolean|distilled.Null When True, this organization allows its data to be used to train PostHog AI models.
---@field is_ai_training_locked? boolean|distilled.Null When True, the AI training opt-out setting cannot be modified through the UI or API.
---@field is_ai_training_cta_shown? boolean|distilled.Null When True, in-app callouts inviting members to enable AI training are shown.
---@field has_signed_baa? boolean Whether the organization has a countersigned Business Associate Agreement on file. When true, AI training stays opted out and cannot be changed.
---@field default_anonymize_ips? boolean Default setting for 'Discard client IP data' for new projects in this organization.
---@field default_role_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the role to automatically assign to new members joining the organization
---@field is_active? boolean|distilled.Null Set this to 'No' to temporarily disable an organization.
---@field is_not_active_reason? string|distilled.Null (optional) reason for why the organization has been de-activated. This will be displayed to users on the web app.
---@field is_pending_deletion? boolean|distilled.Null Set to True when org deletion has been initiated. Blocks all UI access until the async task completes.
---@field uses_most_specific_access_resolution? boolean|distilled.Null When True, access controls resolve with the most specific matching rule. When False, the legacy resolution order applies.

