---@field slack_notification_integration_id? number|distilled.Null ID of the Slack Integration to deliver inbox-item notifications through, or null when notifications are disabled.
---@field slack_notification_channel? string|distilled.Null Where the reviewer ping goes, in the same `id|name` shape PostHog uses elsewhere (only the id is required): a channel (`C0123ABC456|#alerts`), or a workspace member (`U0123ABC456|@sam`) who is sent a direct message. Null disables Slack notifications.
---@field slack_notification_min_priority? posthog.users.SignalUserAutonomyConfigSlackNotificationMinPriority|distilled.Null Minimum report priority that triggers a Slack notification. P0 is highest. Null means notify on every priority. When set, reports without a priority judgment do not notify. * `P0` - P0 * `P1` - P1 * `P2` - P2 * `P3` - P3 * `P4` - P4
---@field github_assign_on_pull_request? boolean Whether to add this user as a GitHub assignee on implementation pull requests for reports that suggest them as reviewer. Off by default. Assignment is additive, so turning it off never removes an assignee from a pull request that already has one.
---@field github_open_pull_request_ready? boolean|distilled.Null Whether implementation pull requests for reports that suggest this user as reviewer open ready for review instead of draft, so the full CI matrix starts right away. Null follows the project's default_open_pull_request_ready. Applies only when the pull request is created; a pull request somebody converts back to draft stays draft.
---@field created_at? string
---@field updated_at? string

---@alias posthog.users.SignalUserAutonomyConfigAutostartPriority posthog.users.AutonomyPriorityEnum|posthog.users.BlankEnum

