---@field uuid? string
---@field first_name? string
---@field last_name? string
---@field email? string

---A cookie-auth login session shown on the user's 'Web sessions' screen.
---@class posthog.users.UserAuthSession
---@field id string Identifier used to revoke this login session.
---@field created_at string|distilled.Null When this login session was first created — the original sign-in time.
---@field last_activity string When this login session last made a request (refreshed periodically).
---@field location string Approximate city and country derived from the IP address, if known.
---@field device string Browser and operating system parsed from the user agent, e.g. 'Chrome 135 on macOS'.
---@field login_method string How this session signed in (e.g. password, Google, SAML).
---@field is_current boolean Whether this is the login session making the current request.

---@class posthog.users.UserCodexAuthTokens
---@field access_token string|distilled.Secret The ChatGPT access token (a JWT) from the `tokens` object of the Codex `auth.json`.
---@field refresh_token string|distilled.Secret The single-use ChatGPT refresh token from the same `tokens` object.
---@field id_token? string|distilled.Null The OpenID id token from the same `tokens` object, when present. Used to read the account email.

---@class posthog.users.UserCodexIntegration
---@field status posthog.users.CodexIntegrationStatusEnum `connected` when cloud runs can use the account; `reauth_required` when OpenAI rejected the refresh token and the user must log in and connect again; `not_connected` when no account is connected. * `connected` - Connected * `reauth_required` - Reauth Required * `not_connected` - Not Connected
---@field plan_type? string|distilled.Null The ChatGPT plan type OpenAI reports for the account.
